      "postedAt": "2026-07-26T08:58:59Z",
      "ingestedAt": "2026-07-26T08:58:59Z",
      "text": "$GOOGL\n reported earnings today:\n\nEPS: $9.11 actual vs $2.91 expected - retail reactions to EPS blowout is kinda just accounting noise, since \n$SPCX\n, Anthropic, and others were likely large contributors. \n\nRevenue: $119.7B actual vs. $116.98B expected\n\nGoogle Cloud Revenue: $24.77B +82% Y/Y, vs. 63-65% expected ($22.2-$22.6B) - this is a very large beat and most material part so far. \n\nCloud Operating Income: ~$8.81B, implying 35.6% margin vs. 32.9% Q1. \n\nCapex: $44.92B vs ~$44.15B (basically in line).\n\nSo initial read through is Google Cloud accelerating growth with expanding margins is genuinely bullish for AI demand.\n\nTheir former $180-$190B capex guidance is already extremely large, and as long as we get around these numbers in the earnings call + forward projections... \n\nShould be good to go for \n$LITE\n and the other optics/networking trade. (eg. last earnings, they said DC and networking would be ~40% of capex spend). \n\nHyperscaler earnings transcripts are probably the most important thing to pay attention to with the AI capex trade. \n\nAnd that should be in 3 minutes.",
      "tickers": [
        "GOOGL",
        "LITE",
        "SPCX"
      ],
      "conviction": "normal",
      "tags": [],
      "views": [
        {
          "ticker": "GOOGL",
          "direction": "bull",
          "why": "Cloud revenue beat by a wide margin with expanding operating margin and capex in line \u2014 genuinely bullish for AI demand",
          "numbers": "Cloud revenue $24.77B +82% Y/Y vs 63-65% expected, cloud operating margin 35.6% vs 32.9%, capex $44.92B"
        },
        {
          "ticker": "LITE",
          "direction": "bull",
          "why": "direct positive read-through as long as capex guidance holds, since DC and networking are roughly 40% of Google's capex spend"
        },
        {
          "ticker": "SPCX",
          "direction": "neutral",
          "why": "named only as a likely contributor to the EPS beat via investment gains, an accounting note rather than a case"
        }
      ],
      "viewsExtractedAt": "2026-08-19T18:36:33Z"
