        "category": "photonics",
        "narrative": "His core theme, and the week it stopped needing his advocacy. He reads a chain of independent confirmations as one story: AXT reporting the largest indium phosphide price hike on record \u2014 a fourth consecutive quarterly increase, with suppliers saying that even with money you may not get material \u2014 Elazr's GM telling an investor conference that the entire supply chain is out of stock and expecting the shortage to run for years across laser chip, PCB, carrier board and packaging, and AOI, Lumentum and MACOM all reporting the same imbalance from the earnings side.\n\nHis framing device is Nvidia as leading indicator. He argues Jensen telegraphs each theme roughly a year early and the market dismisses it every time: Nvidia bought EML and laser capacity in 2025 and the response was that photonics was a bubble; Nvidia is now locking CW and EML capacity with long-term agreements, pushing 800V, and being explicit about the CPO shift, and the response is that CW players are meme stocks. He expects the same resolution.\n\nWithin that he is hunting for who is left. Once Nvidia secures CW capacity he counts AOI, MACOM, Broadcom, Sivers and Semtech as the remaining Western CW players, and calls Sivers the highest-beta exposure and his personal long. On AOI specifically he is at maximum conviction after the Rosenblatt summit \u2014 US-production premiums on 800G and 1.6T, several LTAs declined so capacity is not blocked, sold out through at least H2 next year, and 40%+ margins once CPO arrives \u2014 while saying he wants a materially lower price before adding more.",
        "conviction": "high",
