        "narrative": "His neocloud argument this week is a rebuttal rather than a promotion. CoreWeave signing contracts for six-year-old Nvidia A100 GPUs running through 2029 is, on his read, a direct counterargument to the GPU depreciation short thesis \u2014 if hardware that old still clears multi-year contracts, the aggressive depreciation schedules the bears model are wrong, and that reads positive for Nebius and IREN as much as for CoreWeave.\n\nBeyond that he groups the neoclouds with the other names where demand visibility now runs years rather than quarters, mentioning Nebius in the same breath as AOI in lasers and SanDisk in memory as businesses where the order book extends far enough to change how they should be valued.",
