        "narrative": "Nvidia is less an investment case for him than an information source. His argument is that AI investing is simpler than people expect because Nvidia and Jensen tell everyone what is coming, and markets dismiss it almost every time until it happens. He tracks the forward commitments closely: SB Energy talks, a compute financing push above $500B, Feynman on A16 with custom HBM and co-packaged optics, and an 800VDC MGX rack.\n\nOn AMD he is constructive for structural reasons rather than valuation ones \u2014 Helios plus the CPU line should bring another inflection point, and he notes approvingly that AMD is copying Nvidia's neocloud flywheel by helping fund raises that turn into AMD GPU purchases. He frames it as a second rack-scale accelerator family existing at all, which changes the supplier arithmetic beneath it.\n\nWhat he does not do is argue accelerators on price. The layer functions in his framework as the demand hub whose forward statements validate positions further down the chain.",
